---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title='Omnichannel retail architecture | Marcelo Ojeda';const description='Architecture story: connecting retail channels, ERP, WMS, inventory and logistics as an evolving omnichannel operation.';
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} lang="en"><section class="case-intro"><span class="case-no">ARCHITECTURE STORY / 01</span><h1>From B2B to an omnichannel ecosystem.</h1><p class="lede">The challenge was not adding channels. It was making stores, digital commerce, inventory and logistics behave as one operation while the business kept growing.</p></section><div class="case-facts"><div><small>Context</small><strong>Retail · B2B → Omnichannel</strong></div><div><small>Scale</small><strong>50+ stores · ~800K → ~5M units</strong></div><div><small>Focus</small><strong>Integration · operational continuity</strong></div></div><section class="case-body"><div class="prose"><h2>Growth creates coupling.</h2><div><p>Each new channel adds flows, states and dependencies. Treating e-commerce, marketplaces or stores as isolated projects would have fragmented inventory and fulfillment.</p><p>The architectural work was to evolve the integration between commercial channels and the operational core without losing continuity.</p></div></div><div class="system-flow" aria-label="Conceptual system flow"><span class="node">Channels</span><span class="link">→</span><span class="node accent">Integration</span><span class="link">→</span><span class="node">ERP / WMS</span><span class="link">→</span><span class="node">Logistics</span></div><div class="prose"><h2>Decisions over components.</h2><div class="decision-list"><div class="decision"><b>01</b><strong>Integrate the operation</strong><p>Connect commercial channels with core systems instead of duplicating operational truth.</p></div><div class="decision"><b>02</b><strong>Protect continuity</strong><p>Evolve critical order, inventory, warehouse and dispatch flows while operations remain active.</p></div><div class="decision"><b>03</b><strong>Stay implementation-aware</strong><p>Architecture decisions validated through backend, APIs, databases and enterprise integration.</p></div></div></div></section></BaseLayout>